-fmodules-cache-path claimed where the driver does not use it (no modules, explicit modules), as Xcode 27.0's
driver accepts it without an unused-argument warning in C, Objective-C and C++ compiles, with -fno-modules and with
-fno-implicit-modules (B-170, docs/formats/build.md "Clang's driver"); its other module-only options
(-fimplicit-modules-lock-timeout, -fprebuilt-implicit-modules, -fprebuilt-module-path,
-fmodules-validate-input-files-content, -fmodules-search-all) draw the warning there as here. Written from Xcode's
observed behavior; upstream LLVM leaves the option unclaimed.

